# Media, not source.
#
# The video tooling writes its .avi wherever it is run, and anyone
# converting by hand leaves the downloaded original there too. These run
# about 50 MB per minute - a single four-minute clip is larger than this
# entire repository - and they are usually somebody else's copyrighted
# work besides.
#
# Matched by extension rather than by "*", so the scripts and the
# documentation stay tracked without needing negation rules - which,
# with "last match wins", are how an ignore file quietly stops working.

# what the clock plays
*.avi

# what yt-dlp leaves behind: the source, and its interrupted downloads
*.webm
*.mp4
*.mkv
*.m4a
*.opus
*.part
*.ytdl

# Firmware images. They belong on a release, not in git history, where
# a two-megabyte binary per version would live forever. flash.sh
# downloads them.
*.bin
SHA256SUMS

# editors / os
.vscode/
*.swp
.DS_Store
